==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/lænt/|/lɑːnt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lant.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Etymology 1===
Alteration of earlier {{m|en|land||urine}}, from {{inh|en|enm|*land||urine}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hland||urine}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hland}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hlandą||urine}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*klān-||liquid, wet ground}}. Cognate with {{cog|is|hland||urine}}, {{cog|nn|land||urine}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[aged|Aged]] [[urine]], historically used by the [[Anglo-Saxons]] and others as [[fertilizer]] for high [[nitrogen]] content.
#: {{syn|en|sig}}

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|aged urine}}
* Bulgarian:
{{trans-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[flavor]] ([[ale]]) with aged urine.

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|to flavor with lant}}
* Bulgarian:
{{trans-bottom}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|UK|dialect|Northern England}} {{obsolete form of|en|lanterloo|pos=the card game}}.

===Etymology 3===
Compare {{m|en|lance}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several species of slender [[marine]] [[fish]]es of the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Ammodytes|genus}}, including the common European species ({{taxlink|Ammodytes tobianus|species}}) and the American species ({{taxlink|Ammodytes americanus|species}}).

